[Fix PGXP Wall Edge Kinks]
Description = Straightens kinked and stepped edges on subdivided walls and floors when PGXP is enabled.
Author = Stenzek
Type = Gameshark
Activation = EndFrame
; The game subdivides large polygons close to the camera into a 3x3 grid in object space
; (80019F60), projects the new vertices with RTPT, and then 80019B8C pushes each new edge
; midpoint outward by [1F80000C] = +/-[1F800010] native pixels. On real hardware this hides
; T-junction cracks between subdivided polygons and their unsubdivided neighbours.
;
; PGXP gives the midpoints sub-pixel positions, so the 1px nudge is no longer needed for crack
; hiding and instead shows up as a visible kink along polygon edges (4px at 4x resolution).
; This patch stores 0 to the nudge size in the setup function, so midpoints stay where the GTE
; projected them. Subdivision itself is unchanged. A few single-pixel cracks may remain.
;
; 8001A768: sw s6, 0x10(at) (AC360010) -> sw zero, 0x10(at) (AC200010)
AA01A768 00000001
AC360010 AC200010
